    "question": {
      ":question/id": "d40ed011-a79f-527f-b483-993064167e48",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following augmented matrices have coefficient matrices in row echelon form? Treat the final column of each augmented matrix as its constants column.\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A coefficient matrix, obtained by omitting the final column of its augmented matrix, is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a nonzero row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the preceding nonzero row.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & -3 & 6 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $B$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry in row $2$, column $3$ is in the same column as the leading entry in row $1$, column $3$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $C$ is not in row echelon form since coefficient row $2$ contains only zeros, but row $3$ is nonzero (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, select $A$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "a45084f8-b3c9-54ce-9258-3d29a00a2a92",
          ":answer-field/key": "$A=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & -3 & 6 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right]$",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
