  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186129113,
      "id": "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3",
      "title": "Identifying Augmented Matrices in Row Echelon Form"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "df531cc3-dbc0-5134-bff0-5212e008c014",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following augmented matrices have coefficient matrices in row echelon form? Treat the final column of each augmented matrix as its constants column.\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A coefficient matrix, obtained by omitting the final column of its augmented matrix, is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a nonzero row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the preceding nonzero row.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $A$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry in row $2$, column $2$ is to the left of the leading entry in row $1$, column $3$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 7 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -9\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}10 & 4 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 6 & -8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -6\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, select $B$, $C$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "7915ff17-9509-5df8-a5b0-744f3a926c9c",
          ":answer-field/key": "$A=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 7 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -9\\end{array}\\right]$",
